build
coverage

# NOTE: there is a second .prettierignore at the repo root. lint-staged's
# pre-commit hook runs `prettier --write` from the repo root, which only
# reads *that* file — an exclusion added only here won't stop pre-commit
# from reformatting it (this bit a real commit once; see the root file's
# own note). Both files need the same entry for anything under here that
# must never be reformatted.

# Blog articles migrated from Medium.
# Prettier's markdown reflow damages them: it breaks MDX escape sequences across
# lines (`\{add\}` becomes `\{add\` + `}`, so the escape no longer applies) and
# wraps CJK sentences mid-word, since prose wrapping assumes space-separated
# words. These are content files — there is nothing for a code formatter to fix.
content/blog/

# Golden-test snapshots (scripts/medium-to-mdx/__tests__/golden.test.ts).
# Same failure mode as content/blog/ above: Prettier's markdown formatter
# re-serializes a parsed AST with its own preferred backtick count for inline
# code spans, so a literal ```triple-backtick``` in the snapshot silently
# becomes `single-backtick` on the next `prettier --write .` — a snapshot the
# test itself never wrote, causing the next test run to report a mismatch
# against content the converter never actually produced.
scripts/medium-to-mdx/__tests__/__snapshots__/
